   "etymology": "From the synonym barabar by extraction of bar- as a stem and final -az by analogy with other adverbs such as shkaraz, tërthoraz. Perhaps the stem's extraction as monosyllabic bar- and not also possible disyllabic barab- is due to specific analogy to an adverb like mentioned shkaraz with an also monosyllabic stem and not one like mentioned tërthoraz with a disyllabic stem.\nUltimately from Ottoman Turkish برابر (beraber, baraber), from Classical Persian برابر (barābar, “equal”).",
